1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,303
Night of May 18, 1951,

2
00:00:03,324 --> 00:00:05,364
Yangpyeong, Gyeonggi Province.

3
00:00:05,384 --> 00:00:07,001
Mount Yongmun.

4
00:00:07,389 --> 00:00:09,720
At the headquarters of the Chinese

5
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:11,964
63rd Army there was no doubt.

6
00:00:12,348 --> 00:00:13,747
"The enemy ahead is the same

7
00:00:13,767 --> 00:00:15,719
division we shattered a month ago."

8
00:00:16,106 --> 00:00:17,526
They were not wrong.

9
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:19,429
Just one month earlier,

10
00:00:19,449 --> 00:00:22,378
at Sachang-ri the ROK 6th Division had

11
00:00:22,398 --> 00:00:25,195
collapsed under a Chinese assault.

12
00:00:25,585 --> 00:00:26,981
It abandoned its equipment,

13
00:00:27,001 --> 00:00:29,740
fled over the mountains, and scattered.

14
00:00:30,126 --> 00:00:31,313
So the Chinese committed

15
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:32,985
three divisions at once.

16
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:34,798
Three divisions, against one.

17
00:00:35,190 --> 00:00:37,005
On paper it was a battle that

18
00:00:37,025 --> 00:00:39,264
would be over in a single night.

19
00:00:39,803 --> 00:00:41,223
Yet ten days later,

20
00:00:41,243 --> 00:00:43,736
it was the Chinese who were on the run.

21
00:00:44,136 --> 00:00:45,985
And at the end of that road

22
00:00:46,005 --> 00:00:47,886
a vast lake was waiting.

23
00:00:48,286 --> 00:00:49,538
This is the story of how a

24
00:00:49,558 --> 00:00:51,508
defeated army rose again.

25
00:00:51,598 --> 00:00:54,087
And how one lake came to be called

26
00:00:54,107 --> 00:00:57,136
'The Lake That Defeated the Invaders.'

27
00:00:57,529 --> 00:00:59,830
Spring, 1951.

28
00:00:59,906 --> 00:01:01,833
The Chinese launched what became

29
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:03,973
known as the Spring Offensive.

30
00:01:04,369 --> 00:01:06,145
The first phase came in April.

31
00:01:06,165 --> 00:01:08,337
The second, in mid-May.

32
00:01:08,754 --> 00:01:10,320
The objective was clear.

33
00:01:10,436 --> 00:01:11,782
Drive the United Nations

34
00:01:11,802 --> 00:01:13,728
forces off the peninsula.

35
00:01:13,792 --> 00:01:16,189
At the very least, retake Seoul.

36
00:01:16,587 --> 00:01:18,769
The ROK 6th Division was attached

37
00:01:18,789 --> 00:01:20,589
to the U.S. Ninth Corps.

38
00:01:20,656 --> 00:01:22,935
Its sector: north of Yangpyeong,

39
00:01:22,955 --> 00:01:24,695
around Mount Yongmun.

40
00:01:25,099 --> 00:01:26,731
A rugged peak rising eleven

41
00:01:26,751 --> 00:01:28,636
hundred and fifty-seven meters.

42
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,690
The division commander was

43
00:01:30,710 --> 00:01:33,512
Brigadier General Chang Do-yong.

44
00:01:33,629 --> 00:01:35,192
He used this terrain to set

45
00:01:35,212 --> 00:01:37,537
up an unusual deployment.

46
00:01:37,944 --> 00:01:39,917
Forward, he placed a single unit,

47
00:01:39,937 --> 00:01:42,592
the 2nd Regiment, as an outpost.

48
00:01:42,729 --> 00:01:45,304
Behind it, on the main line of resistance,

49
00:01:45,324 --> 00:01:47,873
the 7th and 19th Regiments.

50
00:01:48,285 --> 00:01:50,662
A forward outpost exists to warn of

51
00:01:50,682 --> 00:01:53,598
the enemy's approach and to buy time.

52
00:01:53,737 --> 00:01:56,431
It is not meant to fight a decisive battle.

53
00:01:56,823 --> 00:01:58,125
On the other side stood

54
00:01:58,145 --> 00:02:00,321
the Chinese 63rd Army.

55
00:02:00,421 --> 00:02:05,604
The 187th, 188th, and 189th Divisions.

56
00:02:06,014 --> 00:02:07,486
Their plan was simple.

57
00:02:07,593 --> 00:02:09,054
Infiltrate by night,

58
00:02:09,074 --> 00:02:11,488
encircle, and break the line.

59
00:02:11,657 --> 00:02:13,833
Just as they had done at Sachang-ri.

60
00:02:14,239 --> 00:02:16,766
But the Chinese did not know one thing.

61
00:02:16,847 --> 00:02:18,852
What the men of the 6th Division had

62
00:02:18,872 --> 00:02:21,534
sworn to themselves in that month.

63
00:02:21,941 --> 00:02:23,758
The night of May 18th.

64
00:02:23,813 --> 00:02:25,977
The Chinese attack began.

65
00:02:26,378 --> 00:02:28,513
Bugles sounded in the darkness

66
00:02:28,533 --> 00:02:30,425
and hundreds, then thousands,

67
00:02:30,445 --> 00:02:32,701
climbed the ridgelines.

68
00:02:33,114 --> 00:02:35,586
They ran straight into the 2nd Regiment.

69
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:37,271
The forward outpost.

70
00:02:37,682 --> 00:02:39,569
And here came the first reversal.

71
00:02:39,977 --> 00:02:42,119
The 2nd Regiment did not fall back.

72
00:02:42,533 --> 00:02:45,111
Under wave after wave of attacks, the 2nd

73
00:02:45,131 --> 00:02:48,138
Regiment was quickly encircled on three sides.

74
00:02:48,563 --> 00:02:50,588
With communications barely holding,

75
00:02:50,608 --> 00:02:53,662
Colonel Song Dae-hoo and his men refused

76
00:02:53,682 --> 00:02:56,269
to yield, and fought to the last.

77
00:02:56,657 --> 00:02:59,578
In response, U.S. Ninth Corps artillery

78
00:02:59,598 --> 00:03:01,650
and supporting units laid down

79
00:03:01,670 --> 00:03:03,608
an unprecedented barrage,

80
00:03:03,628 --> 00:03:05,850
right in front of the friendly positions,

81
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:07,387
and the northern ridges of Mount

82
00:03:07,407 --> 00:03:10,047
Yongmun were pounded through the night.

83
00:03:10,446 --> 00:03:11,809
This was a unit expected to

84
00:03:11,829 --> 00:03:14,278
hold briefly, then withdraw.

85
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:16,644
But the 2nd Regiment held its ground.

86
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:18,692
Surrounded, running low

87
00:03:18,712 --> 00:03:20,840
on ammunition it held.

88
00:03:21,231 --> 00:03:22,822
And so the Chinese command

89
00:03:22,842 --> 00:03:24,772
made a fatal misjudgment.

90
00:03:24,792 --> 00:03:26,348
"They're holding this hard

91
00:03:26,368 --> 00:03:28,277
this must be the main line."

92
00:03:28,672 --> 00:03:30,249
The Chinese kept pouring three

93
00:03:30,269 --> 00:03:32,991
divisions into this one small position.

94
00:03:33,397 --> 00:03:36,188
May 19th, and on into the 20th.

95
00:03:36,311 --> 00:03:39,261
Each night they surged in like waves.

96
00:03:39,281 --> 00:03:43,304
Each dawn they fell back, leaving only their dead.

97
00:03:43,711 --> 00:03:45,736
The 6th Division's records report

98
00:03:45,756 --> 00:03:46,772
the slopes in front of the

99
00:03:46,792 --> 00:03:49,195
position covered with Chinese dead.

100
00:03:49,585 --> 00:03:52,066
And behind that position American

101
00:03:52,086 --> 00:03:54,586
artillery fired without pause.

102
00:03:54,988 --> 00:03:56,136
Three days.

103
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:58,454
For the three days the 2nd Regiment held,

104
00:03:58,474 --> 00:04:00,684
the Chinese were wearing down.

105
00:04:00,774 --> 00:04:02,360
Out of rations, out of

106
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:04,574
ammunition and out of time.

107
00:04:05,113 --> 00:04:07,066
Then came May 21st.

108
00:04:07,117 --> 00:04:08,156
The 6th Division was

109
00:04:08,176 --> 00:04:09,657
ordered to counterattack.

110
00:04:10,073 --> 00:04:11,703
The 7th and 19th Regiments,

111
00:04:11,723 --> 00:04:13,388
waiting on the main line,

112
00:04:13,408 --> 00:04:15,021
moved forward together.

113
00:04:15,424 --> 00:04:16,397
In that moment,

114
00:04:16,417 --> 00:04:18,443
the attacker became the hunted.

115
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:21,572
The exhausted Chinese began to break.

116
00:04:21,696 --> 00:04:23,828
The retreat soon became a rout

117
00:04:23,848 --> 00:04:25,342
and the 6th Division gave

118
00:04:25,362 --> 00:04:26,978
chase without stopping.

119
00:04:27,381 --> 00:04:28,887
Past Gapyeong, along the

120
00:04:28,907 --> 00:04:30,549
Bukhan River, northward.

121
00:04:30,638 --> 00:04:32,289
And at the end of that road

122
00:04:32,309 --> 00:04:33,945
the Hwacheon Reservoir.

123
00:04:34,351 --> 00:04:36,327
Cut off, the Chinese forces were

124
00:04:36,347 --> 00:04:37,954
driven to the water's edge.

125
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:41,004
Deep water ahead. ROK and UN

126
00:04:41,024 --> 00:04:43,322
forces closing from behind.

127
00:04:43,726 --> 00:04:45,563
Many fell here, drowned,

128
00:04:45,583 --> 00:04:47,222
or were taken prisoner.

129
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,822
Pushing north to retake the Hwacheon

130
00:04:49,842 --> 00:04:53,635
power plant and dam, the ROK 6th Division

131
00:04:53,655 --> 00:04:55,934
pressed in from all sides on the Chinese

132
00:04:55,954 --> 00:04:57,989
troops trapped around the reservoir.

133
00:04:58,399 --> 00:05:00,406
Blocked by rugged mountains and cold

134
00:05:00,426 --> 00:05:02,159
water, the retreating enemy's

135
00:05:02,179 --> 00:05:04,493
command structure collapsed entirely,

136
00:05:04,513 --> 00:05:06,690
and the Hwacheon area became the final

137
00:05:06,710 --> 00:05:10,269
graveyard of the Chinese Spring Offensive.

138
00:05:10,646 --> 00:05:12,549
Years later, President Syngman

139
00:05:12,569 --> 00:05:14,996
Rhee gave this lake a new name.

140
00:05:15,221 --> 00:05:16,415
Lake Paro.

141
00:05:16,808 --> 00:05:18,627
Pa, to destroy. Ro,

142
00:05:18,647 --> 00:05:21,242
the invaders. Ho, the lake.

143
00:05:21,636 --> 00:05:23,361
The division defeated just a

144
00:05:23,381 --> 00:05:25,651
month earlier had renamed a lake.

145
00:05:26,047 --> 00:05:28,542
So how did one division hold off three?

146
00:05:28,609 --> 00:05:31,000
Let's break it down into four factors.

147
00:05:31,399 --> 00:05:34,250
First, the deception of the forward outpost.

148
00:05:34,634 --> 00:05:36,429
Because the 2nd Regiment held far

149
00:05:36,449 --> 00:05:38,807
longer than expected, the Chinese

150
00:05:38,827 --> 00:05:41,629
misjudged the main axis of the defense.

151
00:05:41,769 --> 00:05:43,923
With their forces massed in one place,

152
00:05:43,943 --> 00:05:46,074
the two regiments behind it prepared

153
00:05:46,094 --> 00:05:48,949
a counterattack almost untouched.

154
00:05:49,337 --> 00:05:51,707
Intended or not this was the first

155
00:05:51,727 --> 00:05:53,985
move that decided the battle.

156
00:05:54,401 --> 00:05:56,307
Second, firepower.

157
00:05:56,696 --> 00:05:58,541
The Chinese relied on mass,

158
00:05:58,561 --> 00:06:00,815
the so-called human wave.

159
00:06:00,911 --> 00:06:03,167
Behind the 6th Division stood

160
00:06:03,187 --> 00:06:05,921
American artillery and air support.

161
00:06:06,331 --> 00:06:08,909
And the denser the waves climbing the slopes

162
00:06:08,929 --> 00:06:11,676
the heavier the toll the shells would take.

163
00:06:12,075 --> 00:06:13,879
Third, supply.

164
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:16,320
Chinese soldiers fought with the food and

165
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:18,766
ammunition they carried on their backs.

166
00:06:18,787 --> 00:06:21,088
That was enough for roughly one week.

167
00:06:21,497 --> 00:06:23,037
UN forces called it 'the

168
00:06:23,057 --> 00:06:24,697
one-week offensive.'

169
00:06:24,757 --> 00:06:26,672
By the time the 2nd Regiment had

170
00:06:26,692 --> 00:06:28,606
held for three days the Chinese

171
00:06:28,626 --> 00:06:30,409
clock had all but run out.

172
00:06:30,793 --> 00:06:33,736
Fourth, terrain and morale.

173
00:06:33,862 --> 00:06:35,618
Rising above eleven hundred meters,

174
00:06:35,638 --> 00:06:37,948
Mount Yongmun favored the defender.

175
00:06:38,365 --> 00:06:40,601
And above all the 6th Division

176
00:06:40,621 --> 00:06:43,178
carried the scar of Sachang-ri.

177
00:06:43,218 --> 00:06:45,508
The memory of that defeat, and the vow

178
00:06:45,528 --> 00:06:48,770
never to retreat again, held the line.

179
00:06:49,176 --> 00:06:51,182
Official South Korean histories credit

180
00:06:51,202 --> 00:06:52,753
this series of battles with more

181
00:06:52,773 --> 00:06:54,699
than seventeen thousand Chinese

182
00:06:54,719 --> 00:06:57,396
killed and over two thousand captured.

183
00:06:57,526 --> 00:06:59,549
The 6th Division's own losses

184
00:06:59,569 --> 00:07:01,552
numbered in the hundreds.

185
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,463
Of course, wartime figures

186
00:07:03,483 --> 00:07:05,431
are prone to exaggeration.

187
00:07:05,486 --> 00:07:07,196
Claims that 'tens of thousands

188
00:07:07,216 --> 00:07:09,336
drowned' at Lake Paro are treated

189
00:07:09,356 --> 00:07:11,366
with caution by historians.

190
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:13,359
But one fact is clear.

191
00:07:13,459 --> 00:07:15,651
After this battle, the Chinese Spring

192
00:07:15,671 --> 00:07:17,675
Offensive could go no further.

193
00:07:18,082 --> 00:07:20,620
Today, Lake Paro is quiet.

194
00:07:20,716 --> 00:07:21,948
Fishing boats drift,

195
00:07:21,968 --> 00:07:24,154
and mist rises off the water.

196
00:07:24,556 --> 00:07:26,150
But beneath that water

197
00:07:26,268 --> 00:07:28,137
lie the lost years of countless

198
00:07:28,157 --> 00:07:30,610
young men who never came home.

199
00:07:31,031 --> 00:07:32,544
The men of the 2nd Regiment who

200
00:07:32,564 --> 00:07:34,877
held the ridges of Mount Yongmun.

201
00:07:35,044 --> 00:07:37,823
Most of them were around twenty years old.

202
00:07:37,949 --> 00:07:39,625
Ordinary young men who had

203
00:07:39,645 --> 00:07:41,538
left their parents at home.

204
00:07:41,946 --> 00:07:43,446
And the Chinese soldiers

205
00:07:43,466 --> 00:07:44,946
who fell by the lake

206
00:07:45,034 --> 00:07:46,483
were, for the most part,

207
00:07:46,503 --> 00:07:50,063
young men too, sent to a foreign land.

208
00:07:50,608 --> 00:07:52,921
The lesson of Yongmunsan is simple.

209
00:07:52,976 --> 00:07:54,390
A single defeat does not

210
00:07:54,410 --> 00:07:56,142
decide the fate of an army.

211
00:07:56,223 --> 00:07:58,400
And in war, the real weapon

212
00:07:58,420 --> 00:08:00,361
is not numbers alone.

213
00:08:00,766 --> 00:08:02,768
In one month, from a defeated

214
00:08:02,788 --> 00:08:05,099
division to a victorious one.

215
00:08:05,119 --> 00:08:06,937
And in between were the men

216
00:08:06,957 --> 00:08:09,014
who decided to stand again.

217
00:08:09,559 --> 00:08:11,127
If this story meant something to you,

218
00:08:11,147 --> 00:08:13,506
please subscribe and like the video.

219
00:08:13,526 --> 00:08:14,632
We'll continue to bring the

220
00:08:14,652 --> 00:08:16,628
forgotten records of war to light.
